												<div id="earlyAccessHeader" class="early_access_header">
		<div class="heading">
												<h2 class="inset">Early Access Game</h2>
					<p class="inset subtitle">Get instant access and start playing; get involved with this game as it develops.</p>
				
				<p><span>Note:</span> Games in Early Access are not complete and may or may not change further. If you are not excited to play this game in its current state, then you
									should wait to see if the game progresses further in development. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/earlyaccessfaq/?snr=1_5_9_">Learn more</a></p>
					</div>
				<div id="earlyAccessBody" class="devnotes">
							<div class="devs_say">What the developers have to say:</div>
			
			<div id="devnotes_expander">
									<h3>Why Early Access?</h3>
					“We’re releasing Online:404 in Early Access because we plan to continue improving the game, fixing issues, and adding new locations and gameplay mechanics based on player feedback.<br />
<br />
The game is being developed by just two people, and we hope that feedback from the community will help us look beyond our own perspective and discover new ways to improve the game and its mechanics.”
					<h3>Approximately how long will this game be in Early Access?</h3>
					“We plan to bring the game to its final version within 6–12 months.<br />
”
					<h3>How is the full version planned to differ from the Early Access version?</h3>
					“We plan to add new locations, several new survival mechanics, and more ways to interact with zombies and animals. We also plan to introduce full professional voice acting for the characters and continue actively working on bug fixes.<br />
<br />
In addition, we plan to expand the selection of mini-games available on the in-game phone based on feedback from the community.”
					<h3>What is the current state of the Early Access version?</h3>
					“The current version of the game already includes all of the core gameplay mechanics, including everything shown in the trailer.<br />
<br />
The first third of the story is available, along with co-op, resource gathering, building, crafting, hunting, farming, electricity, vehicle driving, zombies and base raids, an in-game smartphone with its own internet, and much more.<br />
<br />
However, players may still encounter bugs and other issues, as it is extremely difficult for a team of our size to identify every problem in a project of this scale on our own. Please report any issues you find using the dedicated bug report form in the pause menu.”
					<h3>Will the game be priced differently during and after Early Access?</h3>
					“We’re offering the game at a reduced price during Early Access as a thank-you to players for their patience and for taking part in the development of the project.<br />
<br />
After the release of version 1.0 and the game’s exit from Early Access, we plan to review the price based on the amount of new content added to the game.<br />
”
					<h3>How are you planning on involving the Community in your development process?</h3>
					“We plan to gather feedback from players and use it to fix bugs and issues, balance gameplay mechanics, and add new features, settings, and mechanics to the game.<br />
”
							</div> <!-- /devnotes_expander -->
			<a class="morebutton" id="devnotes_more" href="#"  onclick="$J('#devnotes_expander').css({'max-height': 'none'}); $J(this).hide(); return false;">Read more</a>
		</div>
	</div>
										
					
